@host = http://localhost:3000
@email = joana.dasilva@example.com
@senha = Senha@123
@novaSenha = NovaSenha@123
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
@userId = {{login.response.body.userId}}
@outroToken = {{login2.response.body.accessToken}}
@outroUserId = {{login2.response.body.userId}}
@resetToken = cole-aqui-o-token-mostrado-no-log

### 1. Cadastro de usuário -> 201 Created
# Os CPFs 11144477735 e 52998224725 são válidos (dígitos verificadores conferem).
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Joana da Silva",
  "cpf": "11144477735",
  "email": "joana.dasilva@example.com",
  "phone": "11987654321",
  "password": "Senha@123"
}

### 1.1. Cadastro duplicado -> 409 CONFLICT
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Joana da Silva",
  "cpf": "11144477735",
  "email": "joana.dasilva@example.com",
  "phone": "11987654321",
  "password": "Senha@123"
}

### 1.2. Cadastro com CPF inválido -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Joana da Silva",
  "cpf": "12345678900",
  "email": "joana.outra@example.com",
  "phone": "11987654321",
  "password": "Senha@123"
}

### 1.3. Cadastro de segundo usuário -> 201 Created
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Carlos Eduardo Souza",
  "cpf": "52998224725",
  "email": "carlos.souza@example.com",
  "phone": "11976543210",
  "password": "Senha@123"
}

### 2. Login -> 200 OK
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "joana.dasilva@example.com",
  "password": "Senha@123"
}

### 2.1. Login do segundo usuário -> 200 OK
# @name login2
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "carlos.souza@example.com",
  "password": "Senha@123"
}

### 2.2. Login com senha errada -> 401 UNAUTHORIZED
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "joana.dasilva@example.com",
  "password": "SenhaErrada@123"
}

### 3. Perfil do usuário autenticado -> 200 OK
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 3.1. Perfil sem token -> 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Accept: application/json

### 4. Solicitar redefinição de senha -> 200 OK
# Sempre 200, exista o e-mail ou não.
# Sem SMTP_HOST configurado o link aparece no log da API (nível Warning).
POST {{host}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "joana.dasilva@example.com"
}

### 5. Redefinir senha com token -> 200 OK
POST {{host}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{resetToken}}",
  "newPassword": "NovaSenha@123"
}

### 5.1. Redefinir senha com token inválido -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{host}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "token-que-nao-existe",
  "newPassword": "NovaSenha@123"
}

### 6. Alterar senha -> 200 OK
# Invalida o token atual: ao final é preciso fazer login novamente.
PATCH {{host}}/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Senha@123",
  "newPassword": "NovaSenha@123"
}

### 6.1. Alterar senha com a senha atual errada -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
PATCH {{host}}/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{outroToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "SenhaErrada@123",
  "newPassword": "OutraSenha@123"
}

### 7. Encerrar sessão -> 200 OK
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 7.1. Reutilizar o token encerrado -> 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 8. Deletar própria conta -> 204 No Content
DELETE {{host}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{outroToken}}

### 8.1. Deletar conta de terceiro -> 403 FORBIDDEN
DELETE {{host}}/api/users/{{outroUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8.2. Deletar conta sem token -> 401 UNAUTHORIZED
DELETE {{host}}/api/users/{{userId}}
